<!-- ABSTRACT -->
<h1 class="center">ABSTRACT</h1>

<p>The <b>Employee Leave Management System (ELMS)</b> is a web-based corporate intranet application engineered to automate, streamline, and centralize the process of requesting, approving, and tracking employee leaves within an enterprise. In traditional paper-based or email-reliant administrative workflows, leave requests often suffer from bureaucratic bottlenecks, lack of operational transparency, manual calculation errors, and fragmented record-keeping. The Employee Leave Management System overcomes these systemic inefficiencies by establishing a secure, auditable, and automated client-server ecosystem connecting staff members directly with administrative leadership.</p>

<p>The application backend is built using <b>Java Servlets (Jakarta Servlet API 6.0)</b> hosted on <b>Apache Tomcat 10.1</b>. In strict adherence to robust enterprise architecture, the presentation tier is rendered dynamically through server-side Java presentation utility classes utilizing servlet response streams, strictly avoiding legacy JavaServer Pages (JSP) and eliminating the network latency associated with bulky front-end CSS frameworks. Relational data persistence is managed via <b>Java Database Connectivity (JDBC)</b> interfacing with a <b>MySQL 8.0</b> database management system.</p>

<p>The system implements comprehensive role-based access control, distinguishing between <b>Employee</b> and <b>Administrator</b> roles. The Employee module allows staff members to register, sign in, apply for leaves across six categorized types (Casual, Sick, Earned, Maternity, Paternity, and Unpaid), monitor approval statuses through intuitive real-time status badges, view managerial remarks, and cancel pending requests. The Administrator module equips managers with live statistical summaries, one-click leave approvals or rejections with custom remarks, complete company-wide leave auditing, and an employee directory. The project represents a complete, scalable, and production-ready enterprise software solution.</p>

