<h1>4. CODING AND IMPLEMENTATION</h1>

<h2>4.1 Project Structure</h2>
<div class="code-block">
fsd2/
├── pom.xml                                      # Build dependencies & WAR packaging
├── build.bat                                    # Automated build batch script
├── deploy.bat                                   # Automated deployment to Tomcat
├── README.md                                    # Setup & user documentation
└── src/
    └── main/
        ├── java/
        │   └── com/leavemanagement/
        │       ├── model/
        │       │   ├── Employee.java            # Employee entity class
        │       │   └── LeaveRequest.java        # Leave request entity class
        │       ├── dao/
        │       │   └── DatabaseHelper.java      # JDBC connection & data access layer
        │       ├── util/
        │       │   └── HtmlTemplate.java        # Dynamic HTML & lightweight CSS generator
        │       └── servlet/
        │           ├── LoginServlet.java         # /login - User authentication
        │           ├── RegisterServlet.java      # /register - Account registration
        │           ├── LogoutServlet.java        # /logout - Session invalidation
        │           ├── DashboardServlet.java     # /dashboard - Employee overview
        │           ├── ApplyLeaveServlet.java    # /apply-leave - Leave application
        │           ├── LeaveHistoryServlet.java  # /leave-history - Employee history & cancel
        │           ├── AdminDashboardServlet.java# /admin-dashboard - Admin action center
        │           ├── ManageLeavesServlet.java  # /manage-leaves - Company leave audit
        │           └── EmployeesServlet.java     # /employees - Staff directory
        └── webapp/
            └── WEB-INF/
                └── web.xml                      # Deployment descriptor (Jakarta EE 6.0)
</div>

<h2>4.2 Database Connection & Schema Management</h2>
<p>The <code>DatabaseHelper.java</code> class implements <code>ServletContextListener</code> and manages the database lifecycle. Upon servlet container startup, <code>contextInitialized()</code> creates the MySQL schema and tables automatically if they do not already exist, and initializes the default administrator account.</p>

<p>Connection parameters are defined as constants at the head of the file:</p>
<p class="no-indent">
• <code>MYSQL_URL</code>: <code>jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/leave_db?createDatabaseIfNotExist=true&useSSL=false&allowPublicKeyRetrieval=true</code><br>
• <code>MYSQL_USER</code>: <code>root</code><br>
• <code>MYSQL_PASS</code>: Configurable database password
</p>

<h2>4.3 User Authentication and Session Management</h2>
<p><b>Registration (<code>RegisterServlet.java</code>):</b> Accepts user details, validates that all fields are populated, enforces email uniqueness in the database, and creates an employee record with <code>role = 'employee'</code>.</p>
<p><b>Authentication (<code>LoginServlet.java</code>):</b> Queries the <code>employees</code> table using a <code>PreparedStatement</code>. Upon verification, an <code>HttpSession</code> is initialized with the authenticated user object. Role-based redirection automatically routes users:</p>
<p class="no-indent">
• <code>role.equals("admin")</code> &rarr; <code>admin-dashboard</code><br>
• <code>role.equals("employee")</code> &rarr; <code>dashboard</code>
</p>
<p><b>Logout (<code>LogoutServlet.java</code>):</b> Terminates the session via <code>session.invalidate()</code> and returns the user to the login screen.</p>

<h2>4.4 Employee Leave Application and Tracking</h2>
<p><b>Application Submission (<code>ApplyLeaveServlet.java</code>):</b> Processes leave submissions. The servlet validates that the end date does not precede the start date (<code>startDate.compareTo(endDate) &lt;= 0</code>) before persisting the request with default status <code>Pending</code>.</p>
<p><b>Dashboard & Metrics (<code>DashboardServlet.java</code>):</b> Queries <code>DatabaseHelper</code> for counts of pending, approved, and rejected leaves, rendering visual summary cards and a quick-view table of recent applications.</p>
<p><b>History & Cancellation (<code>LeaveHistoryServlet.java</code>):</b> Displays an interactive table of all leaves filed by the logged-in user. Any request currently in <code>Pending</code> status displays a "Cancel" button, allowing safe removal.</p>

<h2>4.5 Admin Leave Review and Status Management</h2>
<p><b>Admin Dashboard (<code>AdminDashboardServlet.java</code>):</b> Displays organizational metrics alongside an actionable pending requests table. Each pending record provides inline input for optional remarks and immediate <b>Approve</b> and <b>Reject</b> buttons.</p>
<p><b>Company Management (<code>ManageLeavesServlet.java</code>):</b> Provides full administrative auditing across all historical records, supporting status updates with custom managerial remarks.</p>

<h2>4.6 Employee Directory Management</h2>
<p><b>Directory Inspection (<code>EmployeesServlet.java</code>):</b> Lists all registered personnel with their respective department, system role, pending leave counts, and approved leave totals, giving leadership an immediate high-level view of staff availability.</p>

