<!-- CHAPTER 5 -->
<h1>5. RESULTS AND SCREENSHOTS</h1>

<p>The application was deployed and verified on <b>Apache Tomcat 10.1</b> on <code>http://localhost:8080/leavemanagement/</code>. The following sections describe each verified interface.</p>

<h3>5.1 Login Interface (<code>/login</code>)</h3>
<p>The entrance portal features a clean, focused login card where users authenticate with their registered email address and password. It includes a link to the registration page and a helper box showing administrator demo credentials (<code>admin@company.com</code> / <code>admin123</code>).</p>

<h3>5.2 Registration Interface (<code>/register</code>)</h3>
<p>Provides an intuitive onboarding form where new employees register their Full Name, Email, Password (minimum 4 characters), and Department from a standardized dropdown list (IT Development, Human Resources, Finance & Accounts, Marketing & Sales, Operations, Customer Support).</p>

<h3>5.3 Employee Dashboard (<code>/dashboard</code>)</h3>
<p>Serves as the employee's operational hub. It displays a welcome banner showing their department and email, four colored metric cards (Pending Requests in amber, Approved Leaves in green, Rejected Requests in red, and Total Applications in blue), a shortcut button to apply for leave, and a table of the 5 most recent leave applications.</p>

<h3>5.4 Apply Leave Form (<code>/apply-leave</code>)</h3>
<p>Presents an ergonomic form enabling employees to select from 6 distinct leave types: Casual Leave (CL), Sick Leave (SL), Earned Leave (EL), Maternity Leave, Paternity Leave, and Unpaid Leave / Loss of Pay. Includes HTML5 date controls for Start Date and End Date, a multi-line justification textarea, and server validation ensuring valid date sequencing.</p>

<h3>5.5 Leave History & Cancellation (<code>/leave-history</code>)</h3>
<p>Displays a comprehensive tabular log of all personal leave requests showing leave type, duration, justification, applied date, status badge, and administrator feedback remarks. Active <code>Pending</code> applications feature an interactive red <b>Cancel</b> button with confirmation prompts.</p>

<h3>5.6 Admin Dashboard (<code>/admin-dashboard</code>)</h3>
<p>Provides executive management with high-level summaries: total registered personnel, pending reviews, approved requests, and rejected counts. An actionable review table lists all pending applications, employee details, dates, and justifications, equipped with inline remarks fields and <b>Approve</b> and <b>Reject</b> action triggers.</p>

<h3>5.7 Manage All Leaves (<code>/manage-leaves</code>)</h3>
<p>Offers full visibility over company-wide leave records with detailed status badges (<i>Approved</i>, <i>Pending</i>, <i>Rejected</i>), recorded administrative feedback, and audit timestamps.</p>

<h3>5.8 Employee Directory (<code>/employees</code>)</h3>
<p>Presents an administrative listing of all registered staff members, their departments, assigned privileges, and current leave statistics.</p>

